the attack was launched in the dead of  night a joint assault by America France  and Britain for RAF Tornado bombers  taking off from Akrotiri in Cyprus on a  mission to punish the Syrian regime for  its use of chemical weapons President  Trump announced the airstrikes in a  mid-evening address to the nation  my fellow Americans a short time ago I  ordered the United States Armed Forces  to launch  precision strikes on targets associated  with the chemical weapons capabilities  of Syrian dictator Bashar al-assad a  combined operation with the Armed Forces  of France and the United Kingdom is now  underway  and there was a strong warning to the  countries propping up the Assad regime  Russia and Iran I also have a message  tonight for the two governments most  responsible for supporting equipping and  financing the criminal Assad regime to  Iran and to Russia I asked what kind of  a nation wants to be associated with the  mass murder of innocent men women and  children the nations of the world can be  judged by the friends they keep no  nation can succeed in the long run by  promoting rogue States brutal tyrants  and murderous dictators the night sky  over Syria was lit up by anti-aircraft  fire but there were no reported allied  losses at the Pentagon the American  defense secretary James mattis said the  targets were exclusively chemical weapon  facilities President Trump  directed the US military to conduct  operations in consonance with our allies  to destroy the Syrian regime's chemical  weapons research development and  production capability the chairman of  the Joint Chiefs of Staff Joseph Dunford  was  most specific about the chosen targets  the first target was a scientific  research center located in the greater  Damascus area this military facility was  a Syrian Centre for the research  development production and testing of  chemical and biological warfare  technology the second target was a  chemical weapons storage facility west  of Homs the British tornados returned  safely to Cyprus the strikes were  carefully coordinated with the US and  France Theresa May had this to say this  evening I have authorized British Armed  Forces to conduct coordinated and  targeted strikes to degrade the Syrian  regime's chemical weapons capability and  deter their use we are acting together  with our American and French allies so  there is no practicable alternative to  the use of force to degrade and deter  the use of chemical weapons by the  Syrian regime French jets were also in  action the French president playing a  leading role in pushing for these  strikes he had said last year that the  use of chemical weapons in Syria would  be his redline the Russians who  apparently did not fire on missiles or  aircraft issued a statement through  their ambassador in the United States a  pre-designed scenario is being  implemented he said again we are being  threatened we warned that such actions  will not be left without consequences  all responsibility for them rests with  Washington London and Paris the White  House says it believes sarin and  chlorine were both used in the attack in  Duma last weekend they hope the  airstrikes means such scenes will never  be witnessed in Syria again  if they are then the Americans say more  attacks will follow whatever happens it  is all but certain that the misery of a  brutal civil war is not over yet  mark Austin sky news in Washington
 

